# G085 — Quiz Maker

*v2. See `quiz-maker.md` for prose: round-trip equivalence as the
Files-category contract, line-based text format, polymorphic questions
dispatched through uniform kinds, fold scoring, structured parse errors.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Quiz Archive

[vault-quiz-archive
    IN ORDER TO
        load every .quiz file in the archive directory
        render them as a browseable library
        and persist each user attempt as a text file alongside the quiz

    @files <- [vault[find {path: "quizzes/*.quiz"}]]

    @quizzes <- for @file in @files
        @text <- [fs[read-string {path: @file:path}]]
        @quiz <- [quiz[from-text {text: @text}]]
            || -> #quiz-parse-error {path: @file:path,
                                      reason: @resistance:reason}
        @quiz

    [ui[list-quizzes
          {quizzes: @quizzes indexed-by title}]]

    sync @user-events {
        attempt @quiz-id @answers ->
            @quiz  <- @quizzes where id is @quiz-id first
            @score <- [quiz[score {quiz: @quiz,
                                    attempt: {answers: @answers}}]]
            [vault[save
                    {path: "attempts/" + [clock[now]] + ".attempt",
                     content: [attempt[to-text
                                         {quiz: @quiz,
                                          answers: @answers,
                                          score: @score}]]}]]
    }
]

---

## Verb Surface

[quiz
    new                     {id, title}
    add-mc-question         {quiz, prompt, options, correct-index}
    add-tf-question         {quiz, prompt, correct}
    add-sa-question         {quiz, prompt, expected}
    to-text                 {quiz}                     ;; -> String
    from-text               {text}                      ;; || parse-error
    score                   {quiz, attempt}             ;; -> Score
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: round-trip as a `where` invariant

[quiz[from-text {text: [quiz[to-text {quiz: @q}]]}]
    where the returned quiz is equal to @q
    IN ORDER TO
        guarantee the file format is reliable across writes and reads
        which is the Files category's defining contract
]

The identity `from-text ∘ to-text == identity` is not an assertion in
the demo — it's the property every Files-category verb surface promises
and that downstream choreographies can rely on without checking.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: answer correctness dispatched by `where`

[@question, @answer
    where @question:kind is MC and @answer:kind is MC
        -> [@answer:choice is equal to @question:correct-index]
    where @question:kind is TF and @answer:kind is TF
        -> [@answer:truth is equal to @question:correct-bool]
    where @question:kind is SA and @answer:kind is SA
        -> [@answer:text trimmed and case-folded
             is equal to @question:expected trimmed and case-folded]
    where kinds do not match
        -> #wrong (not #runtime-error)
]

Skipped answers (`none`) are counted separately from wrong answers —
the UI distinguishes "didn't try" from "tried and failed."

---

## Demo

[demo
    @q <- [quiz[new {id: 42, title: "Programming Languages"}]]
    [quiz[add-mc-question
            {quiz: @q, prompt: "Rust's package manager?",
             options: ["npm", "cargo", "pip"], correct-index: 1}]]
    [quiz[add-tf-question
            {quiz: @q, prompt: "Rust has a GC.", correct: false}]]
    [quiz[add-sa-question
            {quiz: @q, prompt: "Ownership model?",
             expected: "ownership"}]]

    @text     <- [quiz[to-text  {quiz: @q}]]
    @restored <- [quiz[from-text {text: @text}]]
    -> @restored is equal to @q                    ;; -> true

    @score <- [quiz[score
                      {quiz: @q,
                       attempt: {answers: [
                          {kind: "mc", choice: 1}
                          none
                          {kind: "sa", text: "  OWNERSHIP  "}
                       ]}}]]
    -> @score:percent                                ;; -> 66.67
]
